# Exactly one root per system: `ν Johnson.PentagonalOrthobirotunda.polyhedron`

`johnsonPentagonalOrthobirotunda_nu_system_<j>`: the systems of `johnsonPentagonalOrthobirotunda_exact` (`Nieuwland.Certs.NieuwlandJohnsonPentagonalOrthobirotunda.Exact`) (here one: the number's minimal polynomial in the interval of its decimals). Each has
**exactly one real solution with every variable in its interval** (`johnsonPentagonalOrthobirotunda_nu_system_<j>_oneRoot`:
`PolynomialSystem.HasUniqueRoot`, `Modules/System/PolyRootOf.lean`), and `ν Johnson.PentagonalOrthobirotunda.polyhedron` is the largest scale among
those roots (`johnsonPentagonalOrthobirotunda_nu_roots_list`). `johnsonPentagonalOrthobirotunda_nu_roots` is the statement in Mathlib's terms alone
(`IsPolyRootMax`, `Modules/System/PolyRoot.lean`), which implies that of the headline `johnsonPentagonalOrthobirotunda_nu`
(`IsPolyRootMax.isPolynomialSystemMax`). The system has one variable, the scale, so its one scale (`johnsonPentagonalOrthobirotunda_exact_list`) is its one root (`PolynomialSystem.IsMaxSingle.isRootMax_of_one_var`).
Generated by `lean/scripts/exact_n.py` from the theorems of `Nieuwland.Certs.NieuwlandJohnsonPentagonalOrthobirotunda` and `Nieuwland.Certs.NieuwlandJohnsonPentagonalOrthobirotunda.Exact`,
which it does not change.
-/

